# Copy to .env and adjust. Never commit .env.
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000

# Local Postgres (Homebrew postgresql@15 on :5432)
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER@localhost:5432/hubworld_dev?schema=public"

# Vite dev server origin, used for CORS
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Xaman (xumm.app) developer credentials. Leave BOTH unset to run sign-in in
# stub mode, which fakes signatures locally so the flow is developable without
# an account. The SECRET is backend-only — it must never reach the frontend.
# The server refuses to boot in stub mode when NODE_ENV=production.
# XAMAN_API_KEY=
# XAMAN_API_SECRET=

# Hubworld's broker account seed. The ONE key Hubworld holds, used only to sign
# the brokered NFTokenAcceptOffer that settles a sale. Backend-only; it must
# never reach the frontend bundle. Without it, listings can be created and
# browsed but sales cannot settle.
# On testnet, generate and fund one with: npm run platform:setup
# PLATFORM_SEED=

# XRPL network: testnet | devnet | mainnet. Defaults to testnet, and it should
# stay there until someone has deliberately decided otherwise — mainnet spends
# real XRP and a mint cannot be undone. Payloads carry force_network from this,
# so a wallet set to mainnet cannot sign a testnet-intended transaction.
# XRPL_NETWORK=testnet

# Where the built frontend lives. Set this in a deploy and Express serves the
# app as well as the API, from ONE origin — which the frontend requires: it
# calls a relative /api, opens its socket with a bare io(), and the SameSite=Lax
# session cookie is not sent on XHR once the API is a different site. Leave it
# unset in dev, where Vite serves the app and proxies /api here.
# The Docker image sets this to /app/public.
# WEB_DIST=/app/public

# Supabase Storage, for event posters. A deploy's filesystem is ephemeral, so
# uploads cannot live on disk.
#
# All optional: leave them unset and POST /api/events/:slug/image answers 503
# while everything else works, so dev needs no bucket. An event without a poster
# renders a generated fallback, which is the normal state rather than an error.
#
# The SERVICE key bypasses row-level security. It is backend-only and must never
# reach the frontend bundle — the same rule as XAMAN_API_SECRET.
#
# Create a PUBLIC bucket named below; posters are shown on public event pages, so
# signing every render would be cost for no privacy.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_BUCKET=event-images

# How Socket.IO shares events between processes.
#
# 'memory' (default) keeps rooms in this process. Correct and fast for ONE
# instance, and silently wrong for two: a client connected to instance A never
# sees a bid published from B. Nothing errors, which is what makes it dangerous.
#
# 'postgres' broadcasts over LISTEN/NOTIFY on the database already in use, so no
# new service is introduced. Turn it on only when running more than one instance;
# a single instance would open a connection it has no use for.
#
# Failing to attach is deliberately NOT fatal — realtime is an accelerator and
# the HTTP API stays authoritative — so watch the startup log to confirm it took.
# REALTIME_ADAPTER=memory
